teach_text = "If there are N liars and N people have the same role, then if you know that there is a liar somewhere else, they must all be innocent."
bottom_out_text = "C1 clears B1, so they have the same role. A2 and B2 cannot both be saying the truth, so at least one of them lies. Since there are only 2 liars, this means B1 and C1 are innocent. B3 says something that has to be true, so they must be a truth-teller. So, there is a liar in column B, and that liar is B2. This means A3 tells the truth. Also, C2 must be telling the truth so as not to create a contradiction. We can deduce that C3 is a truth-teller as well, meaning there is a lying witch, A2."

